@context: When a label appears more than once — NEAR, INSIDE, row with, ON HEADER / ON FOOTER.
@title: which_element

# Three 'Add to cart' buttons, three 'Edit' buttons, two 'Help' links: the label
# alone does not say which. A qualifier names the neighbourhood instead.
@var: {site} = http://localhost:8000

STEP 1: NEAR — the button closest to some text
    NAVIGATE to {site}/shop.html
    CLICK the 'Add to cart' button NEAR 'Manul Plush'
    VERIFY that 'Added Manul Plush' is present
    VERIFY 'Cart total' field has value '24.50'

STEP 2: INSIDE ... row with — one row of a table
    CLICK the 'Edit' button INSIDE 'Team' row with 'Grace Hopper'
    VERIFY that 'Editing Grace Hopper' is present
    CLICK the 'Remove' button INSIDE 'Team' row with 'Alan Turing'
    VERIFY that 'Removed Alan Turing' is present

STEP 3: ON HEADER / ON FOOTER — the same link in two places
    CLICK the 'Help' link ON FOOTER
    VERIFY that 'Help from the footer' is present
    CLICK the 'Help' link ON HEADER
    VERIFY that 'Help from the header' is present

DONE.
